+# Custom kernel additions
+
+The opt-in TP2 collective is implemented in `csrc/xpu/custom_ar/custom_ar.cpp`
+and wrapped by `vllm_xpu_kernels/custom_all_reduce.py`. This addition comes from
+`wyc55069407/vllm-xpu-kernels` commit
+`894c4337ba2519929c9cd7952f082272895f7ee6`. It remains experimental and disabled
+unless the caller explicitly selects it. This document lists the added API;
+it is not a complete inventory of the existing package.
+
+| `_xpu_C` operator | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `custom_ar_create` | Allocate device-side control and communication buffers |
+| `custom_ar_export` | Export local IPC handle information |
+| `custom_ar_open` | Import and verify the peer buffer |
+| `custom_ar_all_reduce_` | Sum contiguous FP16/BF16/FP32 input in place |
+| `custom_ar_error` | Read the bounded-spin error flag |
+| `custom_ar_destroy` | Release the communicator's buffers and IPC mapping |
+| `custom_ar_max_bytes_limit` | Return the native maximum supported size |
